  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed front boundary fence and gate, by reason of their design, height and materials proposed would appear overly dominant and visually intrusive representing an incongruous addition to the subject site and street scene. This would be out of keeping in the immediate context and would detract from the predominantly open character of the surrounding area. Furthermore, the proposal has failed to consider the impact on an existing street tree of amenity value which is likely to be negatively impacted by the proposals.\rThe development is therefore contrary to policy D4 London Plan (2021), policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and policies DMD37 and DMD80 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed front boundary alteration would introduce a secondary dropped kerb which would result in a loss of existing on-street parking capacity detrimental to the availability publicly available vehicle parking provision. Additionally, the increased height of the wall would fall within the sightlines envelope, where any structure should not exceed 0.6m in height. This is considered to have an adverse impact on road safety, particularly for pedestrians and cyclists, and would negatively affect general highway conditions. As such, the proposed scheme is considered to be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2024), Policies DMD46 and DMD47 of the Development Management Document (2014), and Policies CP24, CP25, and CP30 of the Core Strategy (2010).\r"
  ],
